26:player

154:Clearing the Ruins
155:Frieren introduces everyone, and we brief Stark and Fern on the situation so far and what we know about the island.
156:Fern
157:Master {var:player_nickname}, how did you know how to defeat that monster for good?
159:Because the patterns on its body formed a mahjong hand.
161:Once you complete a winning hand, the tiles collapse.
162:Stark
163:Mahjong...? A winning hand...?
164:Ichihime
165:That was Master's special move just now, nyaa!
166:Is that how magic works in your world?
167:You could say that, nyaa! Both mahjong and magic work miracles, nyaa!
168:If you want to learn, I can teach you, nyaa!
169:Learning mahjong seems essential for the journey ahead.
170:We'll be counting on you, Ms. Ichihime, Master {var:player_nickname}.
171:Fern and Stark officially join the party.
172:Exploring ruins, locating crystal balls, transmuting materials... and learning mahjong on the side.
173:Ichihime the Hero and her companions make steady progress across the island.
174:Frieren
175:This mana... It might be a grimoire.
177:No, there's definitely a valuable grimoire inside here. That's what my experience as a mage is telling me.
178:Ms. Ichihime, please help me reason with her... Ah!
180:After much effort, we manage to rescue Ichihime.
181:Now that we know these chests are fake, let's get moving.
182:No... That just means we have even more reason to open the rest.
183:{var:player_nickname}, did you know? Mikheit is only 99% accurate.
184:Historical discoveries have been made by great mages who recognized that remaining 1%... So it's worth another shot.
185:Exactly, nyaa! Probabilities can be deceptive, nyaa!
186:Just because mine was fake doesn't mean Frie's isn't the real deal, nyaa!
187:It's like getting away with a discard only to deal in on the exact same one next turn, nyaa! I know the feeling all too well, nyaa!
188:Why use such a jinxed example...?
189:Yes, she makes a good point. Here I go!
190:Wait!
191:Frieren, don't–
192:But it is already too late.
193:It's so dark and scary in here!
194:And so, the adventure of Ichihime the Hero and her companions continues.
196:Leia
197:Thank you all for your hard work these past few days.
198:Don't mention it. I'm just glad we could be of help.
200:Kaavi
201:Remarkable techniques long thought lost to the currents of fate have been unearthed on this island.
202:Yuzu
203:Argh, even the Red Panda Squad learned how to levitate scoring sticks when declaring Riichi and auto-swap tile backs every match!
206:Yes... Quite a worthwhile trip.
207:Wind, blossoms, snow, and moonlight...? What's that? Sounds pretty fancy...
208:We haven't had a chance to try it out, so no one knows what it actually does yet.
210:Let's ride this momentum and crush the final boss, nyaa!
211:This must be the deepest part of the ruins.
212:Argh? Did you hear that? It sounds like voices...
213:Yes, whispers of fate echo here, but they are too jumbled to decipher.
214:Our target lies among them.
215:That's like fishing out the single winning tile left in the wall, nyaa... Way too hard, nyaa!
216:Spot-on analogy.
217:Anything can happen on this island. It wouldn't surprise me if a tile actually spoke up.
218:So the sound is coming from a mahjong tile? In that case, that spell I found earlier in the ruins might help...
219:N-no! It was just a figure of speech!
220:<color=#6CC2B6>Spell to find the extraordinary mahjong tile!</color>
221:No way... You can't seriously find a mahjong tile with special powers...
222:A giant mahjong tile appears suspended in midair, pulsing with light as if breathing.
223:She actually found one?!
224:I can feel an immense surge of mana. It wasn't there a moment ago...
225:Why does this feel so familiar, nyaa?
226:It doesn't seem evil.
227:It actually feels warm and inviting...
228:This must be the extraordinary mahjong tile.
229:Ms. Frieren, Ms. Ichihime, are these fog-like tethers around the tile a seal?
230:Hm... Hard to say.
231:Feels more like a protective barrier, nyaa.
232:Something is wrong. The magical balance maintaining this place has been shattered...
233:Argh?! What did you do, you phony fortune teller?!
234:Stay sharp, everyone! Prepare for battle!
235:???
236:Gurgle...
237:Just as Leia warned, eerie growls echo through the ruins.
238:Nyaaaa?! The monsters are swarming us like seagulls on a dropped sandwich, nyaa!
239:Master, what do we do, nyaa?
240:Grab the giant tile!
241:Sever those fog tethers!
242:Alright... Here I go!
243:Ms. Frieren, everyone, please lend us your strength!
244:However, with monsters closing in from all sides, we find no easy way to break through.
245:I can't slice through these tethers no matter what I try...
246:Physical attacks aren't working either!
247:The monsters are multiplying. We need to finish this quickly.
248:...But how do we cut them?
249:You're all overthinking this.
250:<color=#70946E>Reelseiden!</color>
251:Monster
252:Grrrgh...!
253:Huh?
254:In an instant, the fog tethers are sliced clean through. The monsters, which had been fiercely guarding the giant tile, suddenly lose their will to fight.
255:Sunlight streams down from the clearing skies as the fog nearby vanishes without a trace.
256:It seems it's all over...
257:I knew following those little monsters would lead to something fun!
258:She just cut right through them so effortlessly...
259:Who are you?
260:Übel
261:Allow me to introduce myself. I'm Übel, a mage.
262:You're a mage, too?
263:That's right.
264:Nyaaa... Judging by her aura, she must be the fourth visitor the Shrine detected, nyaa!
265:I see. So the fourth one is Übel.
266:Hm... So you ended up in this world as well?
267:Thanks for the help, Übel.
268:It was nothing.
269:By the way, I'm quite curious... What exactly is this clear block?
270:Yeah, we fought tooth and nail to get our hands on it, nyaa.
271:Let me take a look...
272:While she examines it, let's head back to camp and resupply.
273:Once everything is sorted, we can return.
274:Some time passes...
275:Oh! So it conceals a formula like this inside.
276:I should take ten years or so to study it thoroughly.
277:Absolutely not.
278:Whoa, hold on, that's way too long...
279:Ms. Frieren, shouldn't we return to camp first? At least to report our findings to Ms. Leia and the others.
280:But the lingering mana traces around here seem worth studying too. I'd like to stay a bit longer...
281:Still, Fern is right. We can't stay here forever. Let's head back to camp first.
282:Either way, light at the end of the tunnel at last, nyaa! Hurrah for us, nyaa!
283:Once the fog finally lifts, we should offer this tile at the Shrine as a souvenir of our adventure, nyaa!
284:Don't celebrate just yet.
285:Nyaa-nyaa?! What is that creepy noise, nyaa...?
287:As she speaks, the calm monsters suddenly grow restless once more.
288:Squishy Slime
289:Gurgle...
290:Man-Eating Mimic
291:Snap...
292:Stranger still, instead of attacking, they scatter in sheer panic.
293:The ground and walls tremble as if struck by an earthquake.
294:This level of shaking... Oh crap!
295:Watch out! The place is coming down!
296:Everyone, run!
297:We can't leave the tile behind after all our hard work, nyaa!
298:...
299:No... Absolutely not.
300:You won't take... my Sacred Tile!
303:But Ms. Frieren, Mikheit has already shown that every chest here is a mimic.
306:As we press on through the island's ruins, the truth behind the fog feels ever closer.
309:It's eating me, nyaa!
310:Don't worry, nyaa! My gut tells me this magic is going to save the day, nyaa!
311:Who knows? Maybe the monsters are gathering again.
319:And it hasn't been without its rewards, nyaa.
320:I've come across some interesting things too. There's this spell to find the extraordinary mahjong tile...
321:And a spell that can create wind, blossoms, snow, and moonlight out of thin air. It was in a well-guarded chest.
